{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.364,
   "text": "Every year, on the first snow, everyone on my street builds a snowman."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.064,
   "end": 13.757,
   "text": "And every year, old Mrs. Pell from next door repeats the same rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.457,
   "end": 18.575,
   "text": "Always build it facing the road... never facing the house."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 19.775,
   "end": 24.319,
   "text": "This was my first winter on Birch Lane, so I built mine alone."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.019,
   "end": 29.072,
   "text": "Coal for eyes. A crooked carrot. My old red scarf."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 29.872,
   "end": 33.157,
   "text": "I turned it toward the road, just like she said."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 34.157,
   "end": 39.725,
   "text": "Around three a.m., I woke up shivering. The heat was off... and the house was silent."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.625,
   "end": 42.972,
   "text": "I went to the front window."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 44.172,
   "end": 46.924,
   "text": "The snowman was facing the house."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 49.324,
   "end": 54.039,
   "text": "I told myself it was just kids. So I went outside, and turned it back."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 55.039,
   "end": 58.025,
   "text": "The next night, I woke up cold again."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 59.025,
   "end": 65.788,
   "text": "This time, the yard was empty. Just round, heavy prints in the snow... leading right up to my front door."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 66.988,
   "end": 68.481,
   "text": "None going back."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 70.481,
   "end": 78.097,
   "text": "This morning, Mrs. Pell asked me where my snowman went. I didn't tell her it's standing in my hallway... facing my bedroom door."
  }
 ],
